Chapter 10, Section 20: "Sheep Mirror, Dog Face"

—Red.

That single color filled Subaru's vision completely.

"—!"

The man in the harlequin mask had appeared suddenly—a figure whose affiliations and intentions were utterly unknown. As a substitute for both a greeting and a farewell, he had hurled a massive fireball at Subaru and the others.

The oppressive heat seared their skin, and the dim sewer became as bright as midday. However, this only served to amplify a certain despair, as the flames spread to fill the narrow waterway, leaving no room to escape and making their advance all too clear to see.

With Crusch on his back and both his once-daily E・M・T and E・M・M already exhausted, the nearly empty Subaru had no means left to deal with this—

"Damn it!"

A rough voice spat out, followed by a viscous splashing sound. At the edge of his vision, Rachins, who had been right beside him, was gone. Like Subaru, he had been shocked by the masked clown's appearance, but he had reacted to the approaching flames faster. —Without any hesitation, he had dived headfirst into the sewage flowing beside the walkway, the only means of escape.

"Subaru! Betty and the others should also—"

"No—"

Seeing Rachins's emergency decision, Beatrice grabbed the hem of Subaru's jersey. With her slight strength and light weight, she tried with all her might to pull Subaru into the sewage.

But Subaru dug in his heels, resisting Beatrice's action. At this unexpected reaction, Beatrice's voice cracked, "Subaru!?" but—

"Trust me, Beatrice."

"—"

Her eyes widened, and Beatrice stared fixedly at Subaru, who had spoken so decisively. Their eyes met, and her round eyes, with their distinctive pattern, trembled as she held her breath.

And then, before she could say anything, the mass of flames loomed right before them. Its overwhelming thermal power would mercilessly burn Subaru, Beatrice, and Crusch on his back to ashes—or so it seemed, but it did not.

"—!"

The flames approached, seared his skin, and felt as if all the moisture in his body would evaporate in an instant. Just as the heat wave seemed about to singe Subaru's bangs, it vanished abruptly.

Like a magic trick, as if the sun before them had been hidden, the sewer's brightness dropped in an instant. All that remained was the lamp in Subaru's hand, the weak light from the fragments of Lagmite ore scattered on the passage floor, and the heated sewer air left by the vanished flames.

—No, that wasn't all.

"—Why?"

"Huh...?"

"Why? How? At this moment, in that spot, in that place... you didn't move?"

The white mask of the harlequin floated in the hazy darkness.

Tilting his head and his mask, the clown looked bewildered. —In fact, he had changed his mask at some point; the villainous face he first showed was gone, replaced by one with X-shaped eyes. Finding this tasteless prank infuriating, Subaru nonetheless blew at his singed bangs and said,

"You mentioned you had business with Crusch-san. So, trying to burn her to death along with the rest of us seemed wrong."

"—. Ku, kuku, kuhahahaha, was that it? That's the only reason you stood your ground? Even though you might have dragged your partner, the Great Spirit, into it too!"

"...But I won the bet."

"What confidence! As expected of the one and only knight of a royal selection candidate! Up till now, and even here, you've carved your path believing in your own decisiveness and insight, is that it!? Amazing, wonderful, I'm in awe! Truly enviable!"

Despite the praising words shouted at him, the masked clown clapped grandly with a voice that held no regard for Subaru at all. As the loud applause, like splitting air, echoed hollowly through the sewer, Subaru gritted his teeth and silently endured the praise-like abuse.

All of that was to avoid needlessly provoking the other party, but—

"What happened just now was the result of Subaru's wisdom surpassing your expectations. To ignore that and resort to petty personal attacks is a truly foolish act, wouldn't you say?"

Instead of the silent Subaru, Beatrice glared sharply and snapped at the man. In response, the masked clown put a hand to his head with a "Tsk-tsk!" and,

"How admirable! How loving! A spirit and their contractor are like a key and a lock fitted perfectly together. Each cannot exist without the other. And that's precisely why! Their bond can be both poison and medicine!"

"You're an impossible person to talk to... It's a nastiness that reminds me of the Sin Archbishops."

"Wait, wait, wait, wait! Spare me, have mercy! Accusing me of all things, a Sin Archbishop! I couldn't bear to be lumped in with those, and anyway, it's you who are suspected of that, right?"

"Suspected? Of what..."

"Of being a Sin Archbishop! That's the rumor going around upstairs, Natsuki Subaru. That you might be the Sin Archbishop of 'Sloth' inside! They're all in a panic, wondering what to do!"

"—!"

Waving his hands flippantly, the masked clown taunted him and swapped his mask back to the original expression. Every little thing he did was irritating, but Subaru had no composure to mention it.

The accusation of being treated as a Sin Archbishop was a heavy burden on Subaru's heart.

"Me, a Sin Archbishop..."

"There's a limit to even absurd suspicion. If that were true, then how do you explain Subaru beating the Witch's Cult to a pulp so far? Would you call it infighting among comrades?"

"Who knows, I don't know, I don't care! No one's interested in the truth anyway. Maybe someone just wants to spread information convenient for themselves, dressed up in a way that benefits them. People like that... are infuriating, aren't they?"

Even while speaking, the masked clown swayed exaggeratedly, unable to stay still. However, just the last added sentence sounded like the true feelings of this eccentric before them.

Feeling that, Subaru took a deep breath in, then exhaled deeply before speaking.

"In the end..."

"Hm? Hmmm? Mmm~?"

"What are you after? I get you're trying to take Crusch-san away. But for what? For whom? In that getup, you can't expect me to believe you're a royal soldier."

Not only were they being pursued by royal soldiers, but the fact they were being treated as Sin Archbishops nearly gave the Sin-Archbishop-allergic Subaru hives, but he put that aside for later.

Focusing the problem solely on the masked clown before him, a natural question arose.

He aimed to secure Crusch's person. But he wasn't an ally of the royal soldiers. —If so, the natural guess was that he was a companion of those who had framed Subaru and the others.

Honestly, even putting aside the matter of Crusch, Subaru and Beatrice, in their empty state, had no chance against an opponent who could wield such powerful magic in a straightforward fight.

They had to somehow extract information, buy time, and find a breakthrough— and it was then.

"—? What's that on you?"

"Hmm~? What is it, what's wrong, if you're buying time... gegeh!"

At Subaru's pointed frown, the masked clown looked down at his own body and groaned.

What Subaru pointed out was the masked clown's black robe, which completely hid his figure—a blinking light faintly visible through the inside of his chest pocket.

Subaru had an idea about the existence of that blinking light.

"Could it be, a 'Communication Mirror'?"

"Ah—! Ee—! Ooh—! Th-there's no way, no reason that would be it, right? Let me tell you! Just because my stomach is flashing doesn't mean your fates are going to—"

"It seems the light's getting stronger. It must be a very important matter."

"Nnngghgh...! You lot! There! In that spot! Wai-i-it right there!"

He declared that vehemently, almost spitting, and the masked clown turned his back on Subaru and the others on the spot. The sight of him so brazenly showing an opening left them completely dumbfounded.

The masked clown, having turned around, rummaged in his pocket and took out something—probably the Communication Mirror—and appeared to start talking with someone through it.

Even showing them his completely unguarded back, Subaru and the others were no threat. It was infuriating to be told that implicitly, but—

"Only got this chance. Hey, pull me up...!"

The lowered voice struck Subaru's ear, having just decided to move, albeit slowly.

Glancing towards the voice, it came from the sewage flowing right beside them—there, Rachins floated with his head above the black water.

"Chin! You were in the sewer this whole time!?"

"I didn't want to carelessly draw that guy's attention! Also, there's a chain sunk in the water, and it's tangled around my leg, I can't get up..."

"If you'd drowned and died there, that would've been the worst way to go."

"Shut up! Just lend me a hand, quickly!"

As Rachins called out from the sewage, Subaru hesitated for a moment about what to do.

Naturally, he wanted to help pull him up, but carrying Crusch on his back filled both of Subaru's hands. In that case, he'd have to rely on Beatrice, but it was doubtful her weight and strength could pull Rachins up. Rather, there was a fear it would just add one more victim to the sewer.

In that case, it might be better to use Murak, which interferes with gravity, and find a parallel breakthrough—

"Ah—, damn it all to hell! I'm doing my job properly! I won't say I haven't been a bit flashy or acted on my own, but I haven't ignored orders or deviated from them or any of that bad-sounding stuff!"

"—!"

Raising his voice, the masked clown stomped his feet and appealed that to the other side of the Communication Mirror.

After that, whatever the person he was talking to told him, he replied with a resigned "Alright, alright!" as if giving in, and then—

"Hey there, catch it without dropping!"

"Huh? — Hey, Beako!"

"—That's dangerous!"

Turning around and dropping his shoulders with a sigh, the masked clown suddenly threw something. The moment Subaru saw it was the Communication Mirror, he called Beatrice's name.

As mentioned, carrying Crusch left Subaru's hands full. So it was Beatrice, hastily reaching out both hands, who caught the object that traced a gentle arc.

"I-I almost dropped it. What are you thinking..."

"The one on the other side of that mirror says they want to talk with you, exchange words!"

"With us?"

The masked clown seemed sulky. At his words, Subaru and Beatrice exchanged looks.

Then, cautiously, wary of any suspicious behavior from the clown, they fearfully peered into the Communication Mirror in Beatrice's hands.

There, on the mirror's surface, the figure of the clown's conversation partner appeared—

'—Oh, you're showing! Um, can you see my face?'

"—"

Seeing the figure reflected in the mirror, Subaru was at a loss for how to react.

He had never expected that the one forming an image in the Communication Mirror handed over by the masked clown would be a girl with a childish face.

She wasn't a familiar face. She was likely a year or two younger than Subaru.

Her long, glossy navy-blue hair was tied up high on both sides, and her large, round golden eyes made a strong impression. Within the narrow frame of the mirror, the girl with refined features and an air that felt somewhat unreliable wore a black jacket over a white shirt decorated with a neat, thin tie at the collar—an outfit that prioritized practicality over glamour, looking at them through the mirror in a black suit.

The gap between the girl's serious gaze and the situation thoroughly confused Subaru.

"You... no, who are you?"

'Um, I am called the "White Sheep." The "Black Dog" there with you... the man in the mask... I am terribly sorry if he has caused you great trouble...'

"S-Sorry..."

The girl who introduced herself as 'White Sheep' bowed deeply on the other side of the mirror. The girl disappeared from the mirror's view with the force of her bow, and Subaru's mind couldn't process the information fast enough.

The masked clown—the man the girl called 'Black Dog'—was clearly a dangerous individual. But this girl, who seemed to be on the same side as 'Black Dog,' bowed her head to Subaru and the others like this—it was either contradictory, incoherent, or a deliberate attempt to confuse them.

"...To be honest, I don't know what to think of you people. My own position is vague as it is, my head and heart are all over the place. Give me something to base a judgment on."

'Something to base a judgment on?'

"If you're an enemy, just say so. —Because I'll smash right through."

"As usual, I suppose."

When Subaru declared that, Beatrice next to him nodded with a defiant face.

As confirmed beforehand, Subaru and Beatrice were currently in a terribly empty state with a severe mana shortage, their hand of cards in tatters. But there was no need to declare that. Even with a hand full of junk, bluffing was a trick to surviving in this other world.

'——'

At Subaru and Beatrice's words, the 'White Sheep' on the other side of the mirror stared wide-eyed.

She was likely the type who showed emotions easily. She seemed to be trying hard to suppress any change in her expression, but the movement of her eyes and facial muscles clearly weren't suited for it.

And the girl, who likely realized this herself every morning facing the mirror, said,

'You say things directly, don't you. ...Aren't you afraid?'

"I am. But it's better when the crisis is right in my own hands. Much better than fumbling around while the crisis rolls somewhere out of my reach."

'—. I'm sorry, once more. The reason 'Black Dog' meddled with you was due to our mishandling and because he was thinking of me.'

"I feel like I'm hearing something selfish and self-righteous there, kuhahahaha."

The masked 'Black Dog' literally feigned ignorance at the 'White Sheep's' apology for her associate's mistake.

Ignoring the 'Black Dog' who was so beyond being worth covering for, the gaze of the girl on the other side of the mirror moved—proof that her attention was drawn to Subaru's back as seen from her side.

Confirming that, the 'White Sheep' gazed at the sleeping Crusch on Subaru's back and said,

'We want to protect... no, secure the person of Crusch Karsten. Because we need that person's power.'

"Crusch-san's power...? You don't mean her left eye?"

Subaru glanced, aware of Crusch's left eye covered by an eyepatch on her back. It was entirely plausible that she was being targeted for that distinct abnormality that had manifested in her, or perhaps for that 'Dragon Eye.' The 'White Sheep' had deliberately corrected herself from 'protect' to 'secure,' probably because she thought expressing it as merely guaranteeing her safety wasn't accurate.

However, betraying Subaru's expectation, the 'White Sheep' asked with a puzzled look, 'Left eye?',

'I haven't been told anything about an eye. What we need is the power of the "Clairvoyance" Divine Protection that Crusch Karsten possesses.'

"—Divine Protection."

'Yes. That power is necessary. —For the fight against the "Beloved Child."'

Thus, with strong determination and resolve, she spoke a phrase he hadn't heard before.












