-













"—For the fight against the 'Beloved Child.'"

The 'White Sheep' had stated that she needed Crusch's Divine Protection for that battle. Unrelated to the 'Dragon Eye' residing in Crusch's left eye, she claimed her goal was merely to secure her person, and Subaru felt a misalignment in the focus of the conversation. To begin with, he had never expected the existence of a completely unknown enemy to be dangled before them here.

"My confusion is starting up again... but what is this 'Beloved Child'?"

"Our enemy. And probably, Natsuki Subaru-san... yours as well."

"...Can I take that to mean it's related to the current pressing situation?"

'—Yes. They are the ones pulling the strings behind the current chaos in the royal capital.'

Her declaration, clearly stating they were the core enemy of this situation, made Subaru hold his breath. Honestly, that declaration from the 'White Sheep' was more welcome to Subaru now than anything. The reality was he had been in the midst of chaos, completely clueless as to who the enemy was or what their objective was. Simply having the information he wanted presented so clearly was enough to raise his favorable impression of the 'White Sheep.'

However—

"If you need Crusch-san for this fight against the 'Beloved Child' and approached us for that, then picking that masked bastard as the negotiator is a colossal failure of personnel selection..."

'N-No, um, well, the royal capital is in quite a tense state right now, and unless someone as capable as 'Black Dog' is around, it's dangerous to even carelessly walk around...'

"A-a-n-d besides, I just happened to tail the right people by chance; I wasn't picked to be the negotiator. So don't go blaming the 'White Sheep' for this, you lot."

"Why do you act so high and mighty about that? Don't tell me that was meant to cover for her? If so, it's not your sense that's lacking, but your understanding of the human heart."

"Kuhahahaha, you little pipsqueak in a sewer-stinking dress. Shall I shut that mouth of yours for good?"

Due to the threatening inferno and his words and actions, Beatrice's hostility toward 'Black Dog' was strong. With 'Black Dog's' mocking retorts added in, he was someone Subaru couldn't feel any goodwill towards either. Moreover, there was a concerning part in what 'Black Dog' just said.

"Did you just say you tailed someone? That means..."

"What a sharp, shrewd one you are, Knight-sama! Indeed, indeed! Searching blindly for a target is a waste of time, energy, and life, right? So I used a different method. I-n o-t-h-e-r w-o-r-d-s, I tailed someone who seemed likely to find them! The one who's in the stinky water now."

"Stinky... water..."

"OI! How long are you bastards gonna chat idly like that!? Enough already, HELP ME!"

Prompted by 'Black Dog' answering while swaying his hips side to side, they looked towards the sewage just as the left-behind Rachins yelled angrily.

It was a huge win that Rachins, familiar with the capital's underbelly, had found Subaru and the others on Felt's orders, but it seemed 'Black Dog' and his companion had taken advantage of that. Still, that only slightly diminished the gratitude he felt towards Rachins. Just slightly.

"Leaving him treading water forever is a bit much. Can we pull him up?"

"Pull him up~? That guy soaked in such filthy, stinking water? I think it would be more hygienic for our discussion to just let him sink as he is."

'... "Black Dog," if you've caused trouble for someone...'

"Alright, a-a-l-r-i-g-h-t! Maybe I bear just a tiny, little bit of responsibility for him jumping in. Maybe I thought just the tiniest bit that it would have been convenient if everyone else got charred black and only the Duchess on your back fell off."

"Before you lower our impression of you any further with more worthless remarks, perhaps you should just get on with it."

The goodwill earned by the still-sensible 'White Sheep' was being ruined by 'Black Dog's' unnecessary comments. With the true intention behind that threatening flame becoming clear, his rating as a dangerous individual increased further.

With that in mind, Subaru and Beatrice took a step back, watching warily as 'Black Dog' reached out a hand to Rachins, who had fallen into the sewage. With his level of magical skill, they couldn't feel safe just because his line of sight was off them.

And that vigilance of Subaru and the others—

"—Huh?"

—proved useful not for 'Black Dog' crouching towards the waterway, but for detecting a different anomaly.

Crack. Somewhere, there was a sound like a fingernail scratching thin porcelain. Reflexively, Subaru's gaze turned towards the sound. —In the depths of the sewer, in the weak light of the Lagmite ore Rachins had thrown at 'Black Dog's' feet and left there, someone's shadow loomed.

"—"

It was a woman.

Wearing a cloak that was neither black nor gray, with wavy deep green hair tucked into its collar, a pale-faced woman with dark, heavy circles under her eyes.

For a moment, Subaru wondered if this woman was also an ally of 'Black Dog' and 'White Sheep'. But before he could question it, the woman moved within his sight.

With one hand hanging limply, she pinched what looked like a white fragment between the fingers of her other hand—her left hand, raised before her chest. The fragment was crushed by the movement of her fingers.

—An instant later, cracks extending from beneath the woman's feet slithered like snakes across the stone paving of the sewer, rushing towards Subaru and the others.

"Uwaaaah!?"

At that terrifying anomaly, Rachins, who had been about to grab 'Black Dog's' hand, shouted.

The racing cracks didn't stop at the floor. They traveled up the walls, to the ceiling, crossing the dirty sewer stones one after another, turning the ancient, damp framework supporting the royal capital's foundation a cloudy white. It was as if everything visible was being replaced with glass.

'—"Black Dog"!'

Amidst the anomaly, it was conveyed to the other side of the mirror, and the 'White Sheep' screamed in a voice close to a shriek. But sadly, no matter how much she raised her voice, she couldn't interfere with Subaru and the others, who were distant beyond the mirror. —However, there was meaning in her raising her voice.

"Don't cry and wail with a trembling voice, I know!"

Because with that single cry, the air of mischievous prank that 'Black Dog' had worn vanished.

He swiftly turned around, boldly standing in the way of the spreading cracks. Subaru could tell that his gaze, which should have been invisible behind the mask, was sharply piercing the woman in the darkness.

Grandly, 'Black Dog' clicked his tongue.

"The worst of the worst! You, of all times, show up here and now!?"

"Someone you know!?"

"Someone I never wanted to know or meet. 'Smasher' Clarissa—the 'Beloved Child'!"

At the name 'Black Dog' spat out, both Subaru and the 'White Sheep' beyond the mirror held their breath. The woman called Clarissa gave no reply. She simply picked up another small fragment from the pouch in her lowered hand. It looked like a pebble.

"Wait, wait, wait, wait, you doing that here—"

'Black Dog' yelled, trying to stop her on the spot, but the stone broke faster.

A clear cracking sound echoed through the sewer—and with that as the signal, the next wave of destruction propagated.

"You've gotta be kidding...!"

A new destruction spread through the already cracked and fissured sewer. The wall right beside Subaru and the others turned a cloudy white, and then, the peeling ceiling came crashing down to crush them.

"Beatrice!"

"I know!"

Responding to his call, Beatrice spread her five fingers towards the collapsing ceiling. Already having used both E・M・T and E・M・M, they were in an empty state where proper combat was difficult. Even so, managing with their insufficient hand was the partnership of Subaru and Beatrice.

"Murak!"

The incantation interfered with reality, and the fragments of the collapsing ceiling took on a pale light, their deadly weight reduced to about that of pumice.

Shielding the sleeping Crusch on his back from the rain of pumice and pulling Beatrice close as well, Subaru leaped far backward—In that instant, the collapse, its weight returned, half-buried the sewer.

"You did it, amazing, pipsqueak! Not a bad split-second decision!"

"If you conveniently got saved along with us, then give us some clear information! That woman is!"

"A Unique Ability user! She breaks things! Destroys them! A gloomy woman who's no fun to talk to! I'm killing her now!"

Benefiting from Beatrice's handling of the situation, 'Black Dog,' who had escaped the collapse, shouted as if laughing, conjured a great wind towards the rubble that had fallen and buried the passage, and unleashed a storm of flying debris into the depths of the corridor.

Without missing its mark, it surged towards Clarissa in the back of the passage—But the moment another light cracking sound was heard, the debris flying through the air shattered, turning to dust by the time it reached her.

"Is that related to breaking those stones?"

Focusing on Clarissa's movements, seeing her left hand drop the crushed stone powder, Subaru guessed that the gesture itself held the logic behind that abnormal destruction. And also, that the pouch Clarissa held still had more pebbles for that purpose.

"Hey, fire! If it's something without substance, she shouldn't be able to stop it by breaking it, right!"

"I see, certainly, but unfortunately! I've already used my fire, it's not in my hand!"

"What!? —Oh, crap!"

At 'Black Dog's' nonsensical rejection, and within Subaru's flustered vision, Clarissa smoothly, with a motion almost like a sacred ritual, pinched the next pebble between her fingers. Already, the floor and walls around Subaru and the others were on the verge of collapse, and if Clarissa broke that fragment, the entire area of the sewer might shatter at once.

At this rate—

"—OI! Over here! Get over here!"

"—!, Chin!?"

At that moment, a desperate call came from the sewage, and Subaru and the others turned around. Looking, they saw Rachins, floating in the water, clinging to the waterway's edge with one hand and pulling something black with the other. —A rusty chain.

Having pulled it up from the water bottom, covered in black mud, Rachins shouted loudly.

"It's a settling tank! Beside the main flow, it's packed full of sludge!"

"Settling..."

Suddenly being given an introduction to the sewer system, an electric current ran down Subaru's spine. A settling tank, accumulated with rotting sludge—that meant the worst possible...

"No way, you...!"

"Heh! You're quick on the uptake, aren't ya."

A terrible sight, his hair plastered to his forehead, soaked in sewage, yet only his four-white eyes gleaming brightly, Rachins laughed at Subaru who had reached the same idea and pulled the chain with all his might.

The rusted, filth-covered chain made a dull sound—and a heavy noise came from the water bottom.

As if in time with that sound, bubbles rose from the water's surface near the wall. What started as small, sporadic bubbles gradually increased in number, making the black water surface suddenly seethe. —In an instant, the air in the sewer, already drifting with a stench, was filled with an overwhelming odor resembling rotten eggs, surpassing the previous smell.

He understood what Rachins was aiming for. There was no time to hesitate.

"Crusch-san is—"

Aware of Crusch sleeping on his back, Subaru momentarily wavered on what to do. Thinking of the action to follow, an unconscious person was far too vulnerable.

In that moment Subaru hesitated, 'Black Dog' moved. —Suddenly, he was shoved.

"You—!"

"This is the right answer, more than being thrown, blown away, and broken!"

Saying this, 'Black Dog' leaped into the sewage all at once, dragging Subaru, Crusch, and even Beatrice with him. Just before they hit the water—suddenly, his vision was covered by something black, and the expected welcome of sewage never came.

Looking, it was a massive, half-formed ball that 'Black Dog' was creating from a clod of earth, trying to wrap it completely around Subaru and the others—

'Please! Trust us!'

In the midst of the urgent situation, the 'White Sheep' reflected on the mirror surface desperately appealed. Pushed by that, Subaru, within the sinking hemisphere of earth, entrusted Crusch's body to Beatrice right beside him, and reached his hand outside the closing ball.

And then—

"—Come on, Rachins!"

"Don't you order me around so high and mighty!"

Having pulled the chain free, Rachins kicked off the wall awkwardly and flew towards them. Subaru grabbed Rachins's outstretched arm and pulled his slender body into the hemisphere in one go.

They tumbled backward, entangled together. Immediately after, the hemisphere completely closed, and almost simultaneously, the faint sound of a pebble fragment being crushed could be heard.

Shaking and a roar could be heard from beyond the thick wall of the closed earthen mass. But beyond that—

"Blow away. —Goa."

Rachins, still piled on top of Subaru, spat that out and snapped his fingers. —Immediately after, a red light was seen spreading through the earthen wall, and the sound and impact arrived a moment later.

"—!?"

A force like being punched from the bottom of his gut shook the world, and Subaru screamed. Even within the water, inside the earthen sphere, it was hot. Blinding. The explosive sound burst, threatening to rupture his eardrums.

"—Ah"

A voiceless scream rampaged inside Natsuki Subaru's body.

Round and round and round and round, heaven and earth spun with terrible force, the submerged earthen sphere was swept away by a violent current, slamming into large objects over and over, getting battered, threatening to knock him unconscious.

What had accumulated in the settling tank was flammable gas produced by a large amount of filth. Rachins had opened the lid of that settling tank, ignited the gas that gushed out in vast quantities, and blown away Clarissa, who had been targeting them, along with the sewer itself. —No, he didn't know what had become of the sewer. He couldn't see. Couldn't hear. Couldn't comprehend.

Just being tossed relentlessly by the surging water and the bouncing earthen sphere, Subaru desperately, tightly, tightly embraced the familiar small sensation and the person he had to protect.

He gritted his teeth and endured. —That was the utmost Natsuki Subaru could do now.

"—"

He gritted his teeth, kept enduring, kept enduring, kept enduring. Until his consciousness was swallowed by the invisible muddy torrent, he just kept, kept enduring—











.........









When he awoke, the first thing he noticed was the smell.

It wasn't the stench of rotten eggs, nor the odor of sewage slathered in filth.

What he smelled was the scent of alcohol and dry cloth. Air warmed without fire passed through his nostrils, and as he breathed it in deeply, feeling an excessive sense of cleanliness—he choked.

"Gehah! Gohoh! Oofeh!"

"Wakyaa, I suppose!"

As Subaru coughed violently and his body jerked, the weight resting on his chest and stomach jerked as well, letting out that adorable little shriek.

He opened his eyes and adjusted the focus of his blurred vision with several blinks. Then, right beside where he lay, he found Beatrice, looking utterly sullen.

Seeing Beatrice with a blanket draped over her shoulders, Subaru's lips trembled.

"Beako... you're safe?"

"Somehow or other, I suppose. Not just a close shave, more like a hundred shaves, perhaps."

"A close shave is about a single hair, so increasing the number changes the meaning... never mind that. More importantly, if you and I are okay, then the others—"

"Calm down, I suppose. Before you get worked up, perhaps look around."

As Subaru leaned forward, his forehead was stopped with a tap by Beatrice's hand. With her small palm pressed against his forehead like that, Subaru moved only his eyes and realized.

Crusch was also laid out on the bed next to the one he was lying on.

"Crusch-san... thank goodness. She's unharmed... right?"

"From what I've heard, she is, I suppose. But she hasn't woken up even once since then. How long the exhaustion from that eye will last is unknown even to Betty, I suppose."

"I see... Ah, Chin's here too. That's a relief."

While relieved to see Crusch on the bed, her chest rising and falling regularly in sleep, beyond her, on a long chair, Rachins was dumped, wrapped up like a mummy in a blanket.

He wasn't awake, but perhaps the chair was uncomfortable, as he frowned in his sleep and mumbled something unintelligible. A wry smile surfaced at the shabby treatment for the man whose quick thinking had saved them, but—

"...Where are we?"

His strength drained by relief, Subaru placed a hand on the bed and finally arrived at that question.

Not only the smell but the appearance told him this was unmistakably somewhere other than the sewer. The stone room had no windows, lit only by a small lamp. A water pitcher, bandages, and folded cloth were neatly arranged beside the bed, and the word "infirmary" vaguely crossed his mind.

"Or maybe a hideout clinic? A back-alley doctor's den..."

"—! You've awakened, Natsuki Subaru-san!"

Immediately after voicing his idle thoughts, a voice, almost like a surprise attack, came from beside him.

When Subaru turned, standing at the entrance to the room was a girl—the person he had seen through the mirror. A girl in a black suit, her long navy-blue hair tied up on the left and right—the 'White Sheep.'

No longer through a mirror, the 'White Sheep' before him clasped her hands in front of her chest, opened them, clasped them again, opened them, repeating this several times before speaking.

"I-I'm so glad... I was so worried that something might have happened to all of you..."

"That's... thank you for worrying about us?"

"Yes! No! Um? Which is it...?"

Unable to decide whether to process apologies, gratitude, or complaints, and in what order, Subaru and the 'White Sheep' both short-circuited in unison.

They had been saved. That was undeniable. But just before that, they had also been threatened by 'Black Dog,' the 'White Sheep's' companion, and the question of what response was correct was endless.

As he was thinking that—

"—'White Sheep,' you mustn't trouble Natsuki-dono. You are supposed to be different from 'Black Dog.' If not, I will need to reconsider our policy."

"—"

The voice came from behind the 'White Sheep,' who was flustered at the room's entrance.

Hearing that voice, seeing the figure of its owner appear, Subaru held his breath and his eyes widened. He should have already consumed more than enough surprises in this single day, yet more were still being added.

Because, once again, the person who appeared alongside the 'White Sheep' was someone Subaru knew.

"You're... Russell-san?"

In a faltering voice, Subaru uttered the name of someone he had ties to long ago—a person he had become acquainted with at the very beginning of the royal selection, whom he had negotiated with to supply support materials for the White Whale subjugation battle immediately after; not someone he had fought alongside directly on the battlefield, but a merchant with whom he had fought the same enemy.

There stood Russell Fellow, bearing the title of representative of the royal capital's merchant guild.

"—"

In his mind, which was at the peak of confusion and chaos, Subaru just stared blankly at Russell, who maintained a composed posture. Meeting Subaru's gaze, the gentleman in a well-tailored suit smiled and nodded deeply.

For some reason, Subaru felt a chill at that smile. —Because it seemed to carry far too many schemes for a mere merchant to wear.

And that premonition of Subaru's proved accurate.

"It was truly fortuitous that we could meet like this, Natsuki-dono. In the face of this unprecedented crisis for the Kingdom, we would very much like to borrow your strength and insight."

"The Kingdom's, unprecedented major crisis..."

"Yes."

Despite the situation being anything but laughable, Russell continued, his smile still in place.

It was—

"—The enemy's aim is the quiet, yet thorough, invasion of the Kingdom. The Kingdom's core has already fallen into the hands of our longtime nemesis, and it is on the brink of ruin."
